Third-party code and content
----------------------------

Every third-party file copied into this repository is listed here with its
source, its licence and its copyright notice (D-036). Dependencies installed
from package registries are declared in pyproject.toml and uv.lock, not copied.

- src/certs/digicert_global_g2_tls_rsa_sha256_2020_ca1.pem
  The public intermediate CA certificate "DigiCert Global G2 TLS RSA SHA256
  2020 CA1" (subject C=US, O=DigiCert Inc; issued by DigiCert Global Root G2;
  valid 30 Mar 2021 to 29 Mar 2031; SHA-256 fingerprint
  C8:02:5F:9F:C6:5F:DF:C9:5B:3C:A8:CC:78:67:B9:A5:87:B5:27:79:73:95:79:17:46:3F:C8:13:D0:B6:25:A9).
  Issued and published by DigiCert, Inc. (one PEM certificate). The file carries
  no licence statement and the repository does not record the URL it was
  downloaded from. It is shipped because www.bger.ch omits it from its TLS
  chain (docs/DATA_LAYER.md); it is used only to verify that chain
  (src/suva_data/sources/bger_lists.py). It is not covered by our licences.

- tests/fixtures/bger_lists/*.html
  Test fixtures saved from the Swiss Federal Supreme Court's website
  (search.bger.ch): 20251212.html is the "Neue Entscheide" (AZA) list page of
  12 Dec 2025, as saved; 20251213.html is the empty response for
  13 Dec 2025; block_page.html is the bot-protection (Imperva Incapsula) page
  the site served instead of a list (its incident id is all zeros). The pages
  carry no licence statement. The rulings they list are official decisions,
  which Swiss copyright law does not protect (Art. 5 para. 1 let. c URG); the
  site's own terms of use apply to the pages themselves. They are not covered
  by our licences.
